warning[L0217]: `shown` binds a Rust path that `display` already binds
 --> check/pattern_implementor_errors.rslisp:1:13
  |
1 | (rust-trait shown "std::fmt::Display" i64 (where ((a shown)) (ref a)))
  |             ^^^^^ this also binds `std::fmt::Display`
  |
  = note: two traits that bind one Rust path can disagree about its implementors
  = help: use `display`, or give `shown` a different Rust path

error[L0404]: `str` does not implement `shown`
 --> check/pattern_implementor_errors.rslisp:6:38
  |
6 | (defn borrowed-text (text) (describe text))
  |                                      ^^^^ this needs `shown`
  |
  = note: `shown` is implemented for: i64, (where ((a shown)) (ref a))

error[L0404]: `unit` does not implement `clone`
 --> check/pattern_implementor_errors.rslisp:9:29
  |
9 | (defn clone-units () (clone (make-pair (do) 1)))
  |                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this needs `clone`
  |
  = note: `clone` is implemented for: bool, char, string, (ref str), i8, i16, i32, i64, i128, isize, u8, u16, u32, u64, u128, usize, f32, f64, (where ((a clone)) (vec a)), (where ((a clone)) (option a)), (where ((a clone) (b clone)) (result a b)), (where ((a clone)) (box a)), (where ((a clone) (b clone)) (pair a b)), (where ((a clone) (b clone)) (pair a b))

error[L0414]: `1` does not fit every type `n` can be
  --> check/pattern_implementor_errors.rslisp:12:19
   |
12 | (defn one (value) 1)
   |                   ^ `n` can be `(ref a)`, which cannot hold this value
   |
   = note: `n` can be any of: i64, (ref a)
   = help: narrow `n` with a trait whose types all hold this value

error[L0404]: `n` might not implement `partial-eq`
  --> check/pattern_implementor_errors.rslisp:15:29
   |
15 | (defn same? (left right) (= left right))
   |                             ^^^^ this needs `partial-eq`
